course: dictionary
lesson: 14669
title: Premise: the idea underneath
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A premise is the idea or fact that something else is built on. In an argument, the premises are the starting points, and they lead to a conclusion. «All dogs need water. Rex is a dog. So Rex needs water.» The first two lines are the premises, and the last line is the conclusion they lead to.
explain: In a story, the premise is the basic idea the whole tale grows from. «The premise of the film is a robot who wants to be a chef.» Every scene follows from that one idea. To find it, ask yourself: what is this story about, in one sentence?
explain: Premises can also mean a building and the land around it. «No dogs are allowed on the premises» means no dogs inside the shop or its grounds. Look at the context: is the sentence about an idea, or about a place?
fact: A premise is an idea or fact that an argument or plan is based on.
fact: The premise of a story or film is its basic idea.
fact: «Premises» (plural) means a building and the land around it, such as a shop or school.
fact: «On the premises» means inside the building or its grounds.
fact: A false premise is a starting idea that is not true, so the reasoning built on it can go wrong.
exercise: «The premise of the story is a girl who finds a talking cat.» What is the premise? | The name of the cat's owner | A list of the page numbers | *The basic idea the story is built on | The last line of the book
exercise: «All cats have tails. Milo is a cat. So Milo has a tail.» Which line is the conclusion? | Cats are soft and furry | All cats have tails | *So Milo has a tail | Milo is a cat
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Smoking is not allowed on the premises.» Where must nobody smoke? | Only in the park | *Inside the building and its grounds | On the bus to school | In the sky above the town
test: «Every bird has feathers. A robin is a bird. A robin has feathers.» Which sentence is the conclusion? | A robin is a bird | Every bird has feathers | *A robin has feathers | Robins are small
test: «The school premises are closed on Sunday.» What is closed on Sunday? | The lessons only | The story's basic idea | *The school building and the land around it | The school's ideas
exam: What is a false premise? | A list of page numbers | A story with a sad ending | A sign that says keep out | *A starting idea that is not true, so the reasoning built on it can go wrong
